<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix17: Ascension Megacorp (AOBA.USAC.Core, workshop 3678583415) lays out the power room of
       USAC_Villa_A as if every building were 1x1:
         1.6/Defs/StructureDef/StructureDef.xml
           :261 Battery            pos (4, 0, 9)
           :265 WoodFiredGenerator pos (5, 0, 9)   ThingRect size (2, 1)
           :316 Battery            pos (4, 0, 10)
           :320 WoodFiredGenerator pos (5, 0, 10)  ThingRect size (2, 1)
       Vanilla footprints are Battery (1,2) and WoodFiredGenerator (2,2), and FFF_Element_ThingRect
       places one copy PER CELL of its rect. So a rect of (2,1) already self-overlaps - two 2x2
       generators one cell apart - and the second row then collides with the first. Fortified
       Features Framework's ErrorCheckAllDefs reports 8 lines over 6 cells:
         (4,0,10) Battery/Battery
         (5,0,10) (6,0,9) (6,0,10) (6,0,11) (7,0,10) WoodFiredGenerator/WoodFiredGenerator
       -> "Two transmitters can't share a cell - PowerNetGrid will error at map generation."
       This is a pre-flight warning at def load; the actual PowerNetGrid failure only happens if the
       villa is selected during map generation.

       The room is walled in at x=3 (Wall :293 / HiddenConduit) and x=7 (Wall :296 / Door), with a
       wall row across z=11 (:299), leaving an interior of exactly x=4..6, z=9..10 - 3x2, six cells.
       The author's four power buildings cannot fit there under any arrangement. One Battery plus
       one WoodFiredGenerator tile it perfectly:
         Battery            (4, 0, 9) occupies x4,    z9..10  = 2 cells
         WoodFiredGenerator (5, 0, 9) occupies x5..6, z9..10  = 4 cells
       So: keep the z=9 Battery, drop the z=10 Battery, drop BOTH generator rects, and add a single
       generator as a plain FFF_Element_Thing. The villa still gets working power; it loses the
       duplicate battery and the generators that were never physically placeable.

       NOTE ON success: deliberately NOT success=Always, unlike most patches here. Fix14 sat dead for
       four days after an upstream restructure precisely because Always hid the mismatch. The
       PatchOperationFindMod wrapper already makes this a no-op when Ascension Megacorp is absent, so
       the only way the inner operations can fail is if the def itself changed shape - which is
       exactly the case we want to be told about. If AOBA fixes the layout upstream this will start
       erroring; that error is the signal to delete this file. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Ascension Megacorp</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- Duplicate battery: 1x2 at (4,0,9) already covers z9..10, so this one collides at z10. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/Fortified.Structures.FFF_StructureDef[defName="USAC_Villa_A"]/elements/li[def="Battery" and pos="(4, 0, 10)"]</xpath>
        </li>

        <!-- Both generator rects. Each is internally overlapping, not just row-vs-row. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
          <xpath>/Defs/Fortified.Structures.FFF_StructureDef[defName="USAC_Villa_A"]/elements/li[def="WoodFiredGenerator"]</xpath>
        </li>

        <!-- One correctly-placed generator filling the remaining x5..6, z9..10. -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/Fortified.Structures.FFF_StructureDef[defName="USAC_Villa_A"]/elements</xpath>
          <value>
            <li Class="Fortified.Structures.FFF_Element_Thing">
              <def>WoodFiredGenerator</def>
              <pos>(5, 0, 9)</pos>
            </li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
